        "narrative": "Macro backdrop \u2014\n[2026-07-23] US economic state (FRED):\n  Growth: real GDP 2.1% (q/q ann)\n  Inflation: CPI 3.23% YoY | core CPI 2.25% | core PCE 2.89% (Fed target 2%)\n  Labor: unemployment 4.2%\n  Rates: fed funds 3.63% | 10Y 4.63% | 10Y-2Y 0.36% (NORMAL)\n  Consumer: UMich sentiment 44.8 | VIX 17.05\n\n---\nRecent market action shows a clear divergence between NQ and ES, with both indices experiencing significant daily declines. The lead-lag analysis indicates that NQ is lagging behind ES, suggesting a rotation out of tech-heavy NQ into broader-market ES. This rotation warning implies caution for NQ traders as the breadth of the market may be shifting away from technology stocks. Volume profiles indicate accumulation zones at 7542-7550 for ES and 29230-29340 for NQ, with price action clustering around these levels. The current volume profile suggests that any significant move below these levels could trigger a re-evaluation of the market dynamics. The upcoming FOMC meeting on July 29th is a key event to watch, as it may influence both indices significantly. Given the mixed signals and the rotation warning, we maintain a short bias with a probability of ~65%, which would be invalidated if NQ breaks above 30,375.",
